---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy — Somwave"
  description="How Somwave handles the information you share with us."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-accent-600">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-ink">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
      This page explains what information we collect and why. We will update it as our services
      evolve.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Information we collect</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink">
      Contact, newsletter, and job application forms collect your name, email address, optional
      phone number, and message. Portal accounts store account details and the associated client's
      project and invoice information.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">How we use it</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink">
      We use this information to respond to you, manage projects and invoices, and protect our
      systems. We do not sell your information to third parties.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Your information</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink">
      Contact us if you want to correct or delete your information.
    </p>
    <h2 id="cookies" class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Cookies</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink">
      The public website saves your navigation language choice in browser storage and a cookie so
      it can be remembered. The client portal uses separate session cookies to keep account access
      secure.
    </p>
    <a
      href="/nala-soo-xiriir"
      class="mt-10 inline-flex h-11 items-center rounded-md bg-primary px-5 text-sm font-semibold text-surface hover:bg-primary-600"
    >
      Contact us
    </a>
  </article>
</PageLayout>
